<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Alestra signs accord with WorldPartners.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Alestra signs accord with WorldPartners.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telephone company Alestra announced an agreement on Wednesday with WorldPartners to market voice and data communications services in Mexico.</p>
<p>&quot;The partnership with Alestra is a decisive step in WorldPartners' market strategy for Latin America, where (the firm) proposes to become market leader...&quot; Alestra said.</p>
<p>Alestra is a joint venture between AT&amp;T, Alfa, Valores Industriales and Grupo Financiero Bancomer.</p>
<p>Mexico's long-distance telephone market will be opened to competition on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Claudia Villegas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9549</p>
</text>
